{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>And I will call in the name of YHWH before you</b> — that I will proclaim before you the great Name that you cannot see. <b>And I will be gracious</b> to whom <b>I will be gracious, and I will show compassion</b> to whom <b>I will show compassion</b> — that through that proclamation you will know the attribute of graciousness and the attribute of compassion, by which they are graced and shown compassion through My Name and My goodness. And concerning this it is said (Numbers 12:7), \"In all My house he is trusted,\" for a man's goodness is in his house."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {0 "The referent of the plural verbs יחוננו וירחמו (\"they are graced and shown compassion\") is left ambiguous in the Hebrew; rendered literally without resolving whether it refers to Israel, to all who pray, or generally."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:20:57.285638025Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}